[agent-assisted] The developer wanted to validate the contradiction detection pipeline against a real-world benchmark of facts that change over time, establishing a recall baseline comparable to the existing DialogNLI results. A new end-to-end benchmark was added that runs 70 knowledge-update pairs through the full extraction and semantic comparison pipeline, achieving 92.9% recall with detailed failure analysis logged in the eval README. The full 277 MB LongMemEval dataset was not evaluated — only the knowledge-update subset from the oracle variant — and the 5 misses (sequence reasoning, niche numeric facts, specific product details) represent a distinct failure mode not yet addressed by the graph or semantic layers.
